WEBVTT

00:41.959 --> 00:45.963
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:49.841 --> 00:53.762
I still find myself
thinking about that moment.

00:54.930 --> 00:55.973
Shoot.

01:07.276 --> 01:09.861
Hyeon Sang-wol! I know you're here.

01:10.696 --> 01:11.905
Come out now.

01:15.200 --> 01:16.243
PRESENTS FROM AMERICA

01:18.036 --> 01:19.204
Hey!

01:19.288 --> 01:21.206
Sang-wol went to the rooftop a minute ago.

01:21.290 --> 01:22.499
- Darn it.
- The rooftop?

01:24.376 --> 01:25.586
Don't "hey" us.

01:28.422 --> 01:30.966
The moment when you,
who devoured every book

01:31.633 --> 01:34.303
and carried around a thick dictionary…

01:36.179 --> 01:37.306
They're gone.

01:38.932 --> 01:41.226
…chose to open
the pages of my book,

01:41.310 --> 01:43.020
pages no one had bothered to read.

01:47.149 --> 01:48.358
There. "Sang-wol."

01:49.109 --> 01:51.903
Lucky you. Ro-sa isn't in here.

01:56.408 --> 01:57.534
Look.

02:01.288 --> 02:03.790
It's okay. From now on, I'll read for you.

02:04.875 --> 02:06.251
"Sangwol."

02:06.335 --> 02:09.588
- "A term for frost and the moon."
- The moment my foggy world…

02:09.671 --> 02:13.550
- "The cold moon on a frosty night."
- …became clear because of your voice.

02:27.439 --> 02:32.736
If you hadn't opened my book then, maybe…

02:32.819 --> 02:34.404
FAMOUS POET KIM RO-SA EXPOSED

02:34.488 --> 02:35.614
…I would never have waited…

02:35.697 --> 02:36.740
POEMS BY KIM RO-SA

02:36.823 --> 02:39.034
…for someone else to read me.

02:39.117 --> 02:43.872
EPISODE 10
READING YOU

02:46.583 --> 02:49.336
Are you sure you'll be okay?
Take a few more days off.

02:49.419 --> 02:50.504
No, I'm good.

02:51.088 --> 02:52.881
I have a lot to do.

02:52.964 --> 02:54.383
Should I go instead?

02:54.466 --> 02:57.552
I'll just say I got a haircut.

02:57.636 --> 02:59.805
Wipe the sleep out of your eyes first.

02:59.888 --> 03:02.182
I'm just worried.

03:02.724 --> 03:05.352
Everyone will be gossiping again at work.

03:05.435 --> 03:07.396
It's fine. My mind is clear now.

03:07.479 --> 03:08.438
See you later.

03:08.522 --> 03:10.774
You really don't want me
to come with you?

03:10.857 --> 03:13.527
What if that jerk is holding a grudge
and is waiting for you?

03:13.610 --> 03:16.154
He's probably too busy
to wait around for me.

03:26.707 --> 03:28.291
Sexual harassment?

03:28.375 --> 03:31.211
Why is she bringing up something
that's already been settled?

03:31.962 --> 03:35.799
Ms. Yu was supposed to be transferred
to the Childal branch.

03:36.425 --> 03:39.469
But the person who filed the report
can't be transferred.

03:40.637 --> 03:42.055
She used the rule to her advantage.

03:42.139 --> 03:46.059
Still, you were unfairly accused.
Why do you have to switch teams?

03:46.143 --> 03:48.520
They're acting like you're guilty
when nothing's been settled.

03:48.603 --> 03:49.813
It is what it is.

03:51.898 --> 03:54.151
It's unfair, but rules are rules.

03:54.693 --> 03:56.611
I'll be back
once the investigation is over.

03:56.695 --> 03:59.364
I know you'll be short-staffed
while I'm away,

04:00.407 --> 04:01.992
but hang in there.

04:02.075 --> 04:04.453
But you just got back.

04:05.620 --> 04:06.913
Here she comes.

04:14.421 --> 04:16.757
Did she… just scoff?

04:18.884 --> 04:21.511
Gosh. What the heck?

04:31.271 --> 04:33.732
I heard you pressed charges
against Mr. Park.

04:33.815 --> 04:35.817
Did something happen?

04:35.901 --> 04:39.070
No. I just finally did the homework
I'd been putting off.

04:40.530 --> 04:42.991
If you ever need help, please let me know.

04:44.242 --> 04:45.619
It won't be right away,

04:46.870 --> 04:49.831
but I plan to do the homework
you gave me too.

04:51.124 --> 04:52.417
Why the change of heart?

04:54.211 --> 04:55.962
Did my sister ask you to?

04:57.422 --> 04:59.883
You know she's not
the type to ask for such a favor.

04:59.966 --> 05:01.510
It was my decision.

05:01.593 --> 05:03.595
So you're in this with me?

05:04.221 --> 05:07.474
But I'll do it my way, at my own pace.

05:07.557 --> 05:11.144
I don't want to lose a fight
I already lost once.

05:14.231 --> 05:15.232
Ta-da!

05:17.526 --> 05:21.238
Here's a little thank-you
for making the trip to the police station.

05:21.321 --> 05:25.951
And this is a bribe
for handling Mi-rae's lawsuit.

05:28.870 --> 05:30.747
There's also a bagel.

05:34.125 --> 05:35.836
Okay. Talk.

05:37.212 --> 05:40.048
You can't just recklessly jump
into a situation like that.

05:40.131 --> 05:42.467
- You should've called me--
- Hey.

05:42.551 --> 05:44.511
I can beat you in a fight easily.

05:45.387 --> 05:47.222
Maybe you can, but that guy…

05:48.139 --> 05:49.891
Beating him
would still be a problem. Listen.

05:49.975 --> 05:52.018
You should settle things
with words or the law,

05:52.102 --> 05:53.353
not with your fists.

05:53.436 --> 05:55.397
What if you had really gotten hurt?

05:55.480 --> 05:57.274
If they'd considered it assault,
you could've--

05:57.357 --> 06:00.277
I get it, mister. Just eat.

06:01.069 --> 06:02.654
I won't do it again.

06:09.786 --> 06:11.037
It's good, right?

06:13.957 --> 06:16.459
What were you even doing there?

06:16.543 --> 06:18.295
Were you on a stakeout or something?

06:18.378 --> 06:19.713
Not at all.

06:19.796 --> 06:21.923
Mom pushed me to come to Seoul, so I did,

06:22.007 --> 06:23.508
and that's what I ran into.

06:23.592 --> 06:25.385
I think she had a hunch.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.888
Maybe it was some
hidden maternal instinct.

06:28.430 --> 06:31.266
So, you'll be staying in Seoul?

06:31.892 --> 06:34.352
Yes, probably for a little while.

06:36.354 --> 06:38.690
You said you felt
like you didn't belong here.

06:39.441 --> 06:41.026
What changed your mind?

06:42.068 --> 06:43.278
I don't know.

06:43.361 --> 06:46.239
I still don't have anything to do here.

06:47.741 --> 06:49.326
Maybe it's because of Mom.

06:49.868 --> 06:51.703
- Your mom?
- Yes.

06:51.786 --> 06:54.831
When I was living in Seoul
without telling Mom,

06:54.915 --> 06:57.083
I felt so uneasy and anxious.

06:57.167 --> 07:00.128
But when she told me to go,
I suddenly felt at peace,

07:00.211 --> 07:02.005
as if I had gotten her permission
or something.

07:02.088 --> 07:03.590
Funny, right?

07:03.673 --> 07:06.217
Since when do I need Mom's permission?

07:06.843 --> 07:10.180
Maybe you just wanted confirmation,
not permission.

07:11.514 --> 07:14.351
That your mom's okay without you.

07:16.186 --> 07:18.563
Why am I like this at 30?

07:19.564 --> 07:23.652
Anyway, for the time being,
get used to seeing me around.

07:26.279 --> 07:29.824
What if… you wake me up crying again?

07:30.992 --> 07:31.910
Hey.

07:33.036 --> 07:34.454
Seriously?

07:36.247 --> 07:37.874
I'm going to eat this.

07:42.212 --> 07:45.298
What do you mean
Mom's not doing well?

07:45.382 --> 07:47.884
It's not that she's sick or anything,

07:47.968 --> 07:50.929
but she doesn't have much energy
and hasn't been eating.

07:51.972 --> 07:54.641
So I was wondering when Mi-ji is coming.

07:55.308 --> 07:57.727
Could she drop by, even just for a bit?

07:57.811 --> 08:00.105
I think she'll eat something
if Mi-ji's here.

08:00.981 --> 08:03.149
That's not Mi-ji's responsibility.

08:03.692 --> 08:07.278
If Mom's not eating,
you should get her to do it.

08:07.362 --> 08:09.489
You know how stubborn she is.

08:09.572 --> 08:12.158
I thought she might listen to Mi-ji.

08:12.659 --> 08:15.495
Mi-ji won't be around for a while.
She's got something to do.

08:15.578 --> 08:16.579
Okay.

08:17.122 --> 08:18.707
Please take good care of her.

08:18.790 --> 08:20.083
All right.

08:20.166 --> 08:21.751
Your mom's not doing well?

08:21.835 --> 08:22.919
Goodness gracious.

08:23.003 --> 08:25.714
Why do you eavesdrop on people's calls?

08:25.797 --> 08:27.966
You were talking loudly.

08:29.384 --> 08:30.969
Where did Mi-ji go?

08:31.761 --> 08:32.887
Seoul.

08:33.430 --> 08:34.514
What? Why is she there?

08:34.597 --> 08:36.391
Does she need to have a reason?

08:37.434 --> 08:39.561
I told her to go and stay with Mi-rae.

08:40.395 --> 08:43.898
Your mom's not doing well.
Ask her to come back for a few days.

08:43.982 --> 08:47.694
Like you said, I'm her daughter,
and Mi-ji's just a granddaughter.

08:49.154 --> 08:50.905
She deserves to live her own life.

08:55.118 --> 08:56.036
What?

08:56.119 --> 08:59.414
Moments like this remind me
of the true purpose of education.

08:59.956 --> 09:01.750
People do change.

09:01.833 --> 09:04.127
Even you can grow as a person.

09:04.753 --> 09:06.671
I'm so proud.

09:07.756 --> 09:11.634
- Are you making fun of me?
- But shouldn't you at least drop by?

09:12.343 --> 09:15.096
When old folks stop eating,
that's serious.

09:15.180 --> 09:16.639
You should get her to eat something.

09:16.723 --> 09:18.975
You can't eat around someone you dislike.

09:19.059 --> 09:20.435
Nothing goes down.

09:20.518 --> 09:22.312
Who does she dislike? You?

09:23.605 --> 09:25.023
Jeez.

09:25.106 --> 09:27.859
Why would you think that?
You're her daughter.

09:27.942 --> 09:29.819
You don't get it.

09:30.570 --> 09:33.364
I can't believe this is happening
right after Mi-ji left.

09:33.448 --> 09:36.451
Don't think like that.
What are you, a teenager?

09:36.534 --> 09:39.162
You're too old now. Go see your mom.

09:39.245 --> 09:41.206
Fine. Let me get back to my business.

09:41.289 --> 09:42.957
You're acting like a kid.

09:44.667 --> 09:46.044
How much is it?

09:46.544 --> 09:48.421
- It's 24,000 won.
- Thanks for the meal.

09:48.505 --> 09:50.048
- It's 24,000 won.
- All right.

09:50.131 --> 09:51.299
Here you go.

09:53.593 --> 09:56.054
- Thanks. It was great.
- Excuse me.

09:56.137 --> 09:59.224
I forgot my glasses today.

09:59.307 --> 10:01.392
- Okay.
- Could you read something for me?

10:01.476 --> 10:02.519
Sure!

10:05.688 --> 10:07.357
You see the poetry book?

10:07.982 --> 10:09.651
This article with the photo.

10:10.193 --> 10:12.028
Let's see.

10:13.613 --> 10:16.616
"Famous Poet Kim Ro-sa Exposed."

10:17.283 --> 10:20.161
"The Talented Ms. Ripley
Who Stole Someone's Entire Life."

10:20.870 --> 10:24.165
"Kim Ro-sa, a poet loved
for her warm lyricism,

10:24.249 --> 10:27.585
is now suspected of being an imposter

10:27.669 --> 10:29.963
living under the name of the late poet."

10:31.005 --> 10:32.924
"An acquaintance from
the late poet's orphanage

10:33.007 --> 10:36.553
allegedly took possession
of her building, royalties, and assets--"

10:37.178 --> 10:39.681
It's nothing special. You can go.

10:39.764 --> 10:42.642
Okay. Thank you.

10:49.149 --> 10:50.316
FAMOUS POET KIM RO-SA EXPOSED

10:50.400 --> 10:54.154
Is this true? You're not spreading
false information, are you?

10:54.237 --> 10:56.948
It's a suspicion based on facts.

10:57.031 --> 10:59.492
Didn't you ask me to do whatever it takes?

10:59.576 --> 11:02.328
But what do we gain
by stirring up this mess?

11:02.412 --> 11:05.623
Making noise in the media
won't change the landowner's mind.

11:05.707 --> 11:07.876
It doesn't look
like she'll change her mind,

11:08.585 --> 11:10.628
so I'm trying to change the owner.

11:11.546 --> 11:12.547
Pardon?

11:13.089 --> 11:14.966
How can we…

11:15.049 --> 11:17.969
The late poet Kim Ro-sa left behind
more than just a name.

11:18.511 --> 11:21.014
There's the restaurant, assets,

11:22.432 --> 11:23.892
and her only son.

11:24.517 --> 11:26.811
They should all go back
to the rightful owner.

11:26.895 --> 11:29.063
Does the son want to sell the building?

11:29.147 --> 11:30.690
His uncle does.

11:31.733 --> 11:33.693
Kim Ro-sa's son is legally incompetent,

11:33.776 --> 11:36.696
so even if he gets the inheritance,
he still needs his guardian's consent.

11:36.779 --> 11:40.325
His uncle volunteered to be his guardian.

11:41.534 --> 11:44.370
An investigative TV show
covering this issue is airing today,

11:44.454 --> 11:46.748
so an official investigation
will begin soon.

11:47.332 --> 11:48.666
Taking legal action…

11:49.584 --> 11:52.545
will probably be much faster
than trying to change her mind.

11:54.589 --> 11:55.632
RESTROOM

12:03.973 --> 12:05.600
What were you talking about?

12:05.683 --> 12:09.020
There's a sign saying
they're hiring, so I asked.

12:09.103 --> 12:11.522
But they want men
because the job requires heavy lifting.

12:11.606 --> 12:14.192
Have you always wanted
to work in a restaurant?

12:14.275 --> 12:17.278
Not at all. I just need to make money.

12:17.362 --> 12:19.572
I have to do something while I'm here.

12:19.656 --> 12:22.075
Then you don't need to rush to get a job.

12:22.158 --> 12:24.661
There are more opportunities
in Seoul than in Duson-ri.

12:24.744 --> 12:28.581
You've done all kinds of part-time jobs,
so you have a lot of options.

12:28.665 --> 12:30.708
Do something you actually want to do.

12:31.209 --> 12:33.586
Mm. Something I want to do?

12:33.670 --> 12:37.298
Is there anything
you're interested in, even just a little?

12:39.634 --> 12:42.929
Do you like being a lawyer?

12:44.847 --> 12:47.058
I wouldn't say I like it…

12:48.434 --> 12:50.436
but I wanted to become one.

12:50.520 --> 12:51.980
Why was that?

12:52.063 --> 12:55.316
You did well in school.
You could've become anything.

12:57.068 --> 12:59.237
This feels like a law school interview.

13:00.029 --> 13:04.117
At the interview,
I said, "to pursue social justice,"

13:04.200 --> 13:05.827
but if I'm being honest…

13:09.247 --> 13:10.873
Because it's a good job?

13:11.499 --> 13:12.875
Do I sound too shallow?

13:12.959 --> 13:15.128
No, it is a good job.

13:16.838 --> 13:21.509
But what if you suddenly couldn't work
as a lawyer anymore?

13:21.592 --> 13:24.512
Like, you couldn't work in law at all.

13:24.595 --> 13:26.514
What would you do?

13:26.597 --> 13:29.392
Is there anything you're interested in,
even just a little?

13:29.976 --> 13:32.395
Okay. I admit I asked
a tough question to answer.

13:32.478 --> 13:36.858
No, don't get me wrong.
I'm just really curious.

13:37.483 --> 13:41.195
I've never thought
about anything else since I quit running.

13:44.866 --> 13:47.327
Then let's try to find out together.

13:47.994 --> 13:51.205
I'll think about
what else I could do besides law.

13:52.373 --> 13:53.374
Okay.

13:58.504 --> 14:00.298
I did plenty
of physical labor, though.

14:00.381 --> 14:02.633
MURDERER STEALS
POET KIM RO-SA'S IDENTITY FOR MONEY

14:49.639 --> 14:50.973
Hello?

14:51.057 --> 14:52.642
I'm Inspector Im Chae-rim

14:52.725 --> 14:56.229
from the Seoul Western District
Prosecutors' Office. Is this Kim Ro-sa?

14:56.312 --> 14:57.397
Yes, this is she.

14:57.480 --> 14:59.982
I'm calling because
you didn't respond to our text.

15:00.483 --> 15:03.778
We'd like you to come in for questioning
regarding a criminal allegation.

15:03.861 --> 15:06.155
Would you be available sometime this week?

15:07.532 --> 15:09.659
A crime? What do you mean?

15:09.742 --> 15:12.161
Numerous tips were received
after the news report.

15:12.245 --> 15:14.747
We're investigating
allegations of identity theft--

15:21.629 --> 15:23.714
POWER OFF

15:36.352 --> 15:38.896
JOB POSTINGS

15:39.689 --> 15:40.898
Come on.

15:40.982 --> 15:42.024
CAREER ROADMAP

15:42.108 --> 15:44.152
Why are you looking at job postings again?

15:44.235 --> 15:46.362
We agreed to just read today.

15:46.446 --> 15:47.655
Look.

15:48.322 --> 15:51.075
Teen Career Guide.
Finding Your Dream in Your Teens.

15:51.159 --> 15:52.493
Career Coaching for Kids.

15:52.577 --> 15:55.079
Just reading the titles makes me anxious.

15:55.830 --> 15:59.000
Do you know what it feels like
to start ten years late?

16:00.293 --> 16:02.336
Don't judge by the titles. Just read them.

16:02.420 --> 16:05.548
I picked out the good ones
after reading them first.

16:05.631 --> 16:07.508
What about you?

16:08.009 --> 16:10.261
You said you were going to look
for careers outside of law,

16:10.344 --> 16:13.055
so what's this?
"Why I Chose a Career in Law"? Seriously?

16:13.681 --> 16:16.350
I couldn't answer your question last time.

16:16.434 --> 16:19.187
Maybe that's why I'm hesitant
about joining A&A.

16:20.771 --> 16:23.524
I figured I should really think about it
before I start officially.

16:23.608 --> 16:24.692
Gosh.

16:25.276 --> 16:26.694
You really live

16:27.236 --> 16:30.490
a tiring, hardworking, but admirable life.

16:31.491 --> 16:34.494
I'll just… keep doing things my way.

16:36.412 --> 16:37.497
Wow!

16:38.039 --> 16:40.374
They pay 150,000 won
for a bioequivalence test? Amazing.

16:40.458 --> 16:44.504
Why don't you try using an app?
Where did you even find these?

16:45.713 --> 16:48.508
Analog has its own special charm.

16:48.591 --> 16:50.051
Print ads feel more…

16:50.927 --> 16:52.470
desperate.

16:52.553 --> 16:54.263
Like they really need me.

16:55.014 --> 16:57.391
Digital ads need you just as much.

16:58.142 --> 17:00.102
Don't be so stubborn.

17:00.853 --> 17:01.979
I'll just…

17:07.944 --> 17:08.986
What is it?

17:09.612 --> 17:10.696
This…

17:11.489 --> 17:13.241
seems to be about Ms. Ro-sa.

17:14.158 --> 17:15.243
What?

17:17.036 --> 17:18.621
POET KIM RO-SA
ACCUSED OF IDENTITY THEFT

17:18.704 --> 17:20.414
FILED A FALSE DEATH REPORT
TO SEIZE ASSETS?

17:23.125 --> 17:26.629
She had a baby and things were fine,
but then she suddenly disappeared.

17:27.296 --> 17:29.757
My whole family
searched the entire country for her.

17:30.383 --> 17:32.343
But when my brother finally found them…

17:33.553 --> 17:34.720
that woman killed him.

17:34.804 --> 17:38.516
After filing her own death report,
the ex-convict took the poet's name.

17:38.599 --> 17:41.644
She put her friend's son
in a psychiatric hospital

17:41.727 --> 17:44.230
and lived as Kim Ro-sa for over 30 years.

17:44.855 --> 17:48.734
The poet's life savings, the royalties
from her best-selling poetry book,

17:48.818 --> 17:52.321
and even the restaurant
she ran to make a living…

17:52.989 --> 17:56.951
The fake Kim Ro-sa took
everything the real one left behind.

17:58.327 --> 18:00.538
A publisher who had met her,

18:01.038 --> 18:04.458
thinking she was
the real Kim Ro-sa, said…

18:07.878 --> 18:09.380
Is this the place from the TV show?

18:09.463 --> 18:11.382
- Must be. Why else would it be closed?
- Oh my.

18:11.465 --> 18:13.634
I ate here a few times.

18:13.718 --> 18:15.177
- Gosh. I've got chills!
- Really?

18:15.261 --> 18:16.262
Goodness.

18:16.345 --> 18:18.598
- How could someone do that?
- I know.

18:18.681 --> 18:21.267
Should a criminal like her
be allowed to run a restaurant?

18:21.350 --> 18:22.560
Of course not.

18:24.562 --> 18:25.730
Ms. Ro-sa.

18:27.857 --> 18:29.233
Are you in there?

18:30.985 --> 18:32.194
I don't think she's home.

18:33.029 --> 18:35.698
What if she collapsed again
and she's on her own?

18:35.781 --> 18:38.909
- Should we call the police?
- No. Ms. Ro-sa!

18:40.369 --> 18:42.371
If you're home, please open the door.

18:44.498 --> 18:45.416
Ma'am.

18:45.499 --> 18:47.001
Ms. Ro-sa.

18:51.172 --> 18:52.923
It's all over now.

18:54.884 --> 18:56.135
Ms. Ro-sa!

19:06.896 --> 19:10.566
This isn't just any case.
It's a sexual harassment case.

19:12.193 --> 19:15.988
If you want, you can take paid leave
until the investigation is over.

19:16.072 --> 19:17.531
Would you like to do that?

19:19.867 --> 19:20.785
No.

19:20.868 --> 19:22.161
Are you sure?

19:22.953 --> 19:24.914
We've separated the other party from you,

19:24.997 --> 19:27.750
but since it happened
within the same department,

19:28.584 --> 19:31.879
things might still get uncomfortable.

19:32.505 --> 19:34.256
If I go on leave now,

19:34.340 --> 19:36.592
everyone will think
I'm running away from this.

19:36.676 --> 19:37.677
I doubt that.

19:37.760 --> 19:39.887
If you stay quiet and out of sight,

19:40.721 --> 19:43.182
people don't believe you.

19:52.441 --> 19:53.484
I'm already swamped,

19:53.567 --> 19:55.486
and I still had to go
to the police station.

19:55.569 --> 19:58.280
What for? The harassment case?

19:58.906 --> 20:00.116
You'll all get called in.

20:00.199 --> 20:02.493
The whole department is a mess
thanks to a nutjob.

20:05.746 --> 20:06.747
What if…

20:08.040 --> 20:10.292
something actually happened?

20:10.376 --> 20:11.335
What do you mean?

20:11.419 --> 20:15.005
It's not just any accusation.
She pressed charges for sexual harassment.

20:15.589 --> 20:17.299
Who would go that far just out of spite?

20:17.383 --> 20:19.135
Didn't you hear what Mr. Park said?

20:19.218 --> 20:22.304
She did it to avoid going to Childal.
That incident was already over.

20:22.388 --> 20:25.224
She just withdrew the complaint.
Nothing was settled.

20:25.850 --> 20:27.476
Something feels off.

20:27.560 --> 20:29.729
What's gotten into you?

20:53.127 --> 20:54.211
Mi-rae!

20:56.464 --> 20:57.631
Se-jin?

20:59.008 --> 21:00.176
I finally found you.

21:09.685 --> 21:11.687
Did you just see that lane change?

21:11.771 --> 21:14.940
I'm not great with stick shifts,
but I'm actually a good driver.

21:15.608 --> 21:17.109
How did you get to Seoul?

21:17.193 --> 21:18.569
I drove my truck.

21:18.652 --> 21:21.489
I nearly died three times on the highway.

21:21.572 --> 21:23.073
Then what about this car?

21:23.157 --> 21:25.159
Remember what you said last time?

21:25.242 --> 21:27.912
That I wouldn't recognize you
if I saw you in Seoul.

21:28.621 --> 21:29.789
That stuck with me,

21:29.872 --> 21:32.291
so I waited around Gwanghwamun
for two days.

21:33.667 --> 21:35.127
But I couldn't find you.

21:35.211 --> 21:38.047
Everyone looked so similar,
with their outfits and hairstyles.

21:38.130 --> 21:41.509
So I figured
it'd be faster for you to find me.

21:41.592 --> 21:44.345
- That's why I brought this car.
- You could've just called.

21:44.428 --> 21:46.055
Mi-ji would've given you my number.

21:46.138 --> 21:49.183
You think I didn't think of that?

21:49.725 --> 21:52.436
That's why I wore sunglasses,
out of embarrassment.

21:52.520 --> 21:57.191
Don't you believe in chance encounters
that feel like fate?

21:57.858 --> 21:59.443
You have no sense of romance.

22:00.653 --> 22:02.321
Why did you want to see me?

22:02.404 --> 22:03.489
Jeez.

22:04.698 --> 22:08.536
You left me hanging
after saying you had something to tell me.

22:09.119 --> 22:11.914
You even promised you'd let me know
before going to Seoul.

22:13.165 --> 22:15.709
Sorry. I had some things to deal with.

22:18.712 --> 22:21.340
Looks like we both have a lot to say.

22:22.216 --> 22:23.801
Can you make time for me tomorrow?

22:24.426 --> 22:27.555
- You can talk now.
- Come on. Just a day.

22:27.638 --> 22:29.515
I came all this way, risking my life.

22:29.598 --> 22:31.267
Let's just think of it
as a one-day workshop

22:31.350 --> 22:33.060
and spend a day together, okay?

22:33.727 --> 22:35.604
Will you show up in this car?

22:35.688 --> 22:38.941
- Will you meet me if I do?
- No. Only if you leave it behind.

22:39.692 --> 22:41.777
Then we'll spend the entire day together.

22:41.861 --> 22:43.320
Wait, the entire day?

22:43.404 --> 22:45.364
You want me to bring this car?

22:46.073 --> 22:47.449
See you in the morning.

22:48.534 --> 22:50.744
This car is not supposed to be a threat.

22:51.412 --> 22:54.123
When did driving cars like this one
become a bad thing?

23:16.395 --> 23:17.605
What's so funny?

23:18.731 --> 23:20.274
So this is your usual look.

23:21.859 --> 23:23.819
Let's go. We don't have much time.

23:24.737 --> 23:25.821
Hello.

23:25.905 --> 23:28.365
Gosh, Se-jin! Long time no see.

23:28.449 --> 23:29.783
This is my business partner.

23:29.867 --> 23:30.951
Nice to meet you.

23:31.035 --> 23:32.578
- Here, take this.
- No, I…

23:32.661 --> 23:33.954
Take it. It suits you.

23:34.038 --> 23:35.289
It's pretty.

23:35.372 --> 23:38.292
- She got this to celebrate your opening.
- Oh, right.

23:39.168 --> 23:40.169
Thank you.

23:42.922 --> 23:44.006
It's sweet.

23:45.591 --> 23:47.009
This is my business partner.

23:47.092 --> 23:48.928
Nice to meet you.

23:49.595 --> 23:51.096
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

23:53.766 --> 23:54.808
It's so good.

23:54.892 --> 23:58.354
Jeez, who comes to a brewery
and drinks Coke?

23:58.437 --> 23:59.855
Enjoy, Mi-rae.

24:01.357 --> 24:04.735
You seem to know
all the owners wherever we go.

24:04.818 --> 24:07.154
It's not that I know the owners.

24:07.237 --> 24:08.781
My friends became the owners.

24:09.740 --> 24:11.200
They were all office workers.

24:11.283 --> 24:13.494
But now they're running
their own businesses.

24:13.577 --> 24:17.081
Looks like things worked out for everyone.

24:17.164 --> 24:19.833
Don't even get me started.
Every time we drank,

24:19.917 --> 24:23.337
they'd cry about why nobody
stopped them from quitting their jobs.

24:23.420 --> 24:26.382
Even that one was barely scraping by
until last year.

24:26.465 --> 24:30.135
The chocolate shop owner's first shop
went under, so that is his second.

24:31.387 --> 24:33.722
They're all amazing.

24:33.806 --> 24:35.891
I wonder where they get the courage.

24:35.975 --> 24:38.894
I know. Where does it come from?

24:41.105 --> 24:42.856
I guess that's the thing.

24:43.941 --> 24:46.568
They all started from the bottom,

24:46.652 --> 24:48.779
so even if they hit rock bottom again,

24:48.862 --> 24:51.490
they believe they can climb back up.

24:53.450 --> 24:55.327
This really is a workshop.

24:55.995 --> 24:57.287
You wanted me to see them.

24:59.289 --> 25:03.127
Originally, I just wanted to show you
what it means to throw money around.

25:03.627 --> 25:06.463
But your reaction to the car
wasn't great, so I switched gears.

25:08.590 --> 25:11.552
You said you had no one in Seoul
to give strawberries to.

25:11.635 --> 25:13.804
I wanted you to meet some nice people.

25:16.265 --> 25:19.476
Now that you've met them,
put whatever you want on my tab.

25:21.520 --> 25:22.563
Cheers.

25:28.527 --> 25:30.320
I think I'm getting drunk.

25:31.864 --> 25:33.323
Did you spike this?

25:37.995 --> 25:40.664
I tried, but she's not eating.

25:42.499 --> 25:44.835
Please convince your mom to eat.

25:51.467 --> 25:52.676
Oh dear.

25:53.385 --> 25:55.596
Look at you eating so well.

25:55.679 --> 25:57.556
How about one more bite?

25:57.639 --> 25:58.682
Hey.

25:58.766 --> 26:00.225
What are you doing?

26:00.726 --> 26:01.602
You're here.

26:02.603 --> 26:04.521
Ok-hui's here.

26:06.190 --> 26:07.775
A FLAVOR KIDS LOVE

26:09.401 --> 26:10.944
Ok-hui.

26:12.529 --> 26:15.616
Are you still mad?

26:16.533 --> 26:19.119
Am I someone who's always angry?

26:26.335 --> 26:30.547
Why did you butt in without telling me?
That was unnecessary.

26:30.631 --> 26:31.882
Jeez.

26:31.965 --> 26:35.385
You butted into my business first.
Is it only "unnecessary" when I do it?

26:35.469 --> 26:37.638
I brought pine nut porridge.
Feed her later.

26:39.264 --> 26:43.018
Old people are just like babies
when it comes to feeding them.

26:43.727 --> 26:45.854
Try to get her to eat gently.

26:45.938 --> 26:48.398
Maybe even smile while you're at it.

26:49.942 --> 26:53.070
I've never even done that
for my own kids. How can I…

26:53.821 --> 26:56.156
Well, I've never raised a baby.

26:56.782 --> 26:58.784
If I can do it, why can't you?

27:07.876 --> 27:09.711
She wasn't like this before.

27:12.256 --> 27:15.717
Haven't you heard that everyone
turns into a child when they get old?

27:16.385 --> 27:17.636
She's no exception.

27:18.554 --> 27:20.389
Not my mom.

27:21.140 --> 27:23.851
She didn't shed a tear
when she got kicked out by my dad.

27:23.934 --> 27:26.937
Instead, she yelled at me
for not walking fast enough.

27:30.315 --> 27:33.026
I'd never seen that expression
on her face before.

27:35.279 --> 27:38.615
But the thought of her hiding
that expression all this time…

27:41.076 --> 27:44.037
makes me wonder
what I've been resenting all my life.

27:50.794 --> 27:54.923
You're lucky it's not too late.

28:00.053 --> 28:01.388
I never got

28:02.514 --> 28:04.725
much love from my mom either.

28:07.978 --> 28:10.814
Those new clothes I got every season?

28:11.690 --> 28:12.649
Jeez.

28:13.150 --> 28:16.862
My mom thought
I wasn't as good as my sisters,

28:16.945 --> 28:20.949
so she always dressed me well
to save herself the shame.

28:25.287 --> 28:28.790
All my life, I'd been sidelined.

28:29.333 --> 28:34.046
It wasn't until I met Ho-su's dad
that I knew what it was like to be loved.

28:36.131 --> 28:38.217
Once I felt that, I finally understood.

28:39.885 --> 28:41.637
Gosh.

28:41.720 --> 28:45.098
You have to be loved…

28:45.766 --> 28:47.726
to know how to love.

28:48.894 --> 28:51.021
Then, later on, this thought hit me.

28:52.272 --> 28:53.482
"If…

28:54.524 --> 28:57.277
I had loved my mom first…

29:04.493 --> 29:07.788
would she have loved me back?"

29:12.793 --> 29:16.546
It's too late for me,
but not for you, Ok-hui.

29:18.173 --> 29:20.550
Give her some love before it's too late.

29:21.969 --> 29:23.053
Okay?

29:35.148 --> 29:37.859
POET KIM RO-SA
ACCUSED OF IDENTITY THEFT

29:45.659 --> 29:47.619
That's way too detailed.

29:49.454 --> 29:50.914
Who on earth…

29:54.251 --> 29:56.169
Ho-su, come sit. Quick.

29:56.670 --> 29:58.088
What's going on?

29:59.506 --> 30:01.633
Did you get in touch with Ms. Ro-sa?

30:03.343 --> 30:07.014
First, promise me you won't get mad.

30:07.097 --> 30:08.557
Why would I…

30:10.309 --> 30:12.019
Don't tell me you picked the lock.

30:13.270 --> 30:14.980
That's illegal…

30:15.772 --> 30:16.857
What is this?

30:17.983 --> 30:19.609
SEOUL WESTERN DISTRICT
PROSECUTOR'S OFFICE

30:19.693 --> 30:20.819
The prosecutor's office?

30:21.486 --> 30:22.362
Where did you…

30:22.446 --> 30:24.448
I went through the trash.

30:24.531 --> 30:28.410
I swear, I was just trying to see
when she'd left the house.

30:28.493 --> 30:29.995
Then I found this.

30:30.537 --> 30:31.997
No, put it back.

30:32.080 --> 30:33.749
And then what?

30:33.832 --> 30:36.335
She threw it away
without even knowing what it was.

30:36.418 --> 30:38.670
If it's important, we should let her know.

30:38.754 --> 30:39.963
Even if she threw it away,

30:40.047 --> 30:42.090
that's theft, a violation of privacy,
and illegal.

30:42.174 --> 30:44.384
It's not the time
to worry about legal stuff.

30:44.468 --> 30:46.970
Does the law know that she can't read?

30:47.054 --> 30:48.472
Does the prosecutor's office know?

30:48.555 --> 30:50.182
Only we know.

30:50.265 --> 30:51.641
She didn't ask us for help.

30:52.392 --> 30:54.227
We don't exactly know what's going on.

30:54.311 --> 30:56.021
I'm not sure if we should jump in--

30:56.104 --> 30:58.732
Not everyone can ask for help.

30:59.399 --> 31:02.778
Mi-rae didn't tell me about
her situation either until I found out.

31:03.695 --> 31:06.406
We have family, but Ms. Ro-sa has no one.

31:06.490 --> 31:08.533
She probably doesn't even know
how to ask for help.

31:08.617 --> 31:12.204
Is it right to leave her alone
just because she didn't say anything?

31:13.080 --> 31:15.499
I'm going to start breaking…

31:16.416 --> 31:20.504
that privacy law or whatever right now.

31:20.587 --> 31:24.966
I'm reading it out loud to myself.
This has nothing to do with you.

31:25.050 --> 31:27.511
If you don't want to hear it,
cover your ears.

31:28.136 --> 31:29.930
"Regarding the criminal case

31:30.013 --> 31:32.808
involving forgery of private documents,
among other charges,

31:32.891 --> 31:36.311
you are requested to appear at Prosecutor
Ko Yeong-hak's office, Room 503."

31:36.395 --> 31:39.272
"It is alleged that you used
another person's name for your own benefit

31:39.356 --> 31:41.817
- for a considerable period--"
- Wait.

31:42.609 --> 31:44.403
What's the prosecutor's name?

31:46.530 --> 31:47.697
Ko Yeong-hak.

31:50.409 --> 31:52.077
PROSECUTOR KO YEONG-HAK'S OFFICE

32:01.545 --> 32:04.381
Sir, what brings you here?

32:04.464 --> 32:06.216
Is Mr. Lee here right now?

32:06.842 --> 32:07.926
Yes.

32:11.555 --> 32:13.306
Sir, you can't go in.

32:17.269 --> 32:18.478
It's fine.

32:20.230 --> 32:21.398
Ho-su.

32:22.023 --> 32:23.400
What brings you here?

32:23.942 --> 32:25.569
Thinking about coming back?

32:25.652 --> 32:27.404
Were you behind everything?

32:28.655 --> 32:31.241
What exactly are you referring to?

32:31.324 --> 32:33.952
You orchestrated
the news articles and TV coverage.

32:34.035 --> 32:37.372
And isn't Prosecutor Ko Yeong-hak,
who's conducting the investigation,

32:38.123 --> 32:39.916
your closest friend from law school?

32:40.959 --> 32:42.627
Are you saying I pulled strings?

32:44.045 --> 32:45.380
Without any grounds,

32:46.089 --> 32:47.716
that's a dangerous thing to say.

32:49.843 --> 32:51.636
Do you really have to go this far?

32:51.720 --> 32:53.096
Rosa Restaurant…

32:53.972 --> 32:56.641
is just one of the many cases you handle.

32:57.726 --> 33:00.979
Why are you targeting someone
with no family or friends?

33:01.563 --> 33:03.064
Why are you so angry?

33:04.983 --> 33:07.027
Did I fabricate a crime?

33:08.445 --> 33:10.530
Ms. Kim Ro-sa… No.

33:10.614 --> 33:14.659
Ms. Hyeon Sang-wol's wrongdoings
are only now coming to light.

33:14.743 --> 33:15.660
Sir!

33:15.744 --> 33:17.579
Again, this is the problem with you.

33:18.830 --> 33:22.959
Do you think the law applies differently
to the poor or those without family?

33:23.668 --> 33:26.129
Or are you blindly defending your client?

33:27.130 --> 33:29.508
Then you should've done the same
for Chairman Choi.

33:30.425 --> 33:31.551
Do you…

33:33.720 --> 33:37.057
really think Chairman Choi
and Ms. Kim Ro-sa are comparable?

33:37.140 --> 33:38.725
What makes them so different?

33:38.808 --> 33:41.353
As lawyers, we should see them as equals.

33:43.230 --> 33:44.356
By the way,

33:44.940 --> 33:47.859
it's Ms. Hyeon Sang-wol, not Kim Ro-sa.

33:49.194 --> 33:51.446
You should get your client's name right.

34:01.706 --> 34:03.875
Are you okay? Ho-su.

34:06.670 --> 34:10.382
If I'd known what kind of person you are,
I wouldn't have come today.

34:12.467 --> 34:14.386
I don't think I'll be coming back.

34:26.565 --> 34:27.816
Ms. Ro-sa.

34:28.733 --> 34:31.278
If you're home, please come out.

34:32.904 --> 34:34.155
Ms. Ro-sa!

34:35.991 --> 34:37.325
Hey, Ho-su.

34:37.409 --> 34:38.743
KFMC was behind this.

34:38.827 --> 34:41.121
They started the scandal
because of the restaurant.

34:41.204 --> 34:43.748
What does the restaurant
have to do with it?

34:43.832 --> 34:46.293
If the identity theft charges stand,
the ownership could change.

34:46.376 --> 34:48.503
In place of her son,
who's in the nursing home,

34:48.587 --> 34:51.506
they'll probably appoint a guardian
they've already set up.

34:51.590 --> 34:52.716
A guardian?

34:54.259 --> 34:55.885
I'll call you back soon.

35:02.601 --> 35:04.436
What do you mean I can't?

35:04.519 --> 35:07.439
It's against our policy
to take that type of payments.

35:07.522 --> 35:11.151
I mean… I'm just trying to pay

35:11.234 --> 35:14.571
for several months in advance.
Why is that a problem?

35:15.655 --> 35:17.407
Are you really his family?

35:18.658 --> 35:19.576
What?

35:19.659 --> 35:22.954
Ever since that show aired,
we've been flooded with calls.

35:23.038 --> 35:25.624
Someone claiming to be his family
showed up the other day.

35:25.707 --> 35:28.585
It's putting us
in a really difficult position.

35:34.382 --> 35:38.053
I… have my reasons.

35:38.136 --> 35:40.764
If you could just let me pay in advance--

35:40.847 --> 35:44.768
I'm telling you I can't.
No matter how much you insist, I can't.

35:46.645 --> 35:47.937
Why not?

35:48.688 --> 35:51.024
It's not like she's asking for money.

35:51.107 --> 35:52.734
What's the reason for saying no?

35:52.817 --> 35:56.112
She said she has her reasons.
Does she have to beg?

35:56.196 --> 35:57.947
It's against our policy--

35:58.031 --> 36:00.950
What policy? Does it even exist?

36:01.034 --> 36:02.535
If it does, show me.

36:03.953 --> 36:07.540
Why were you just standing there?
That's not like you.

36:08.166 --> 36:10.001
What do you know about me?

36:10.543 --> 36:11.544
About you?

36:11.628 --> 36:14.255
You shout, you argue,
and you throw salt at people.

36:14.339 --> 36:16.800
You're not the type
to just stand there and take it.

36:16.883 --> 36:18.176
You haven't done anything wrong--

36:18.259 --> 36:19.969
Because that's who I really am.

36:20.053 --> 36:21.888
Because I'm not Kim Ro-sa!

36:29.437 --> 36:31.147
You must've heard it too.

36:32.816 --> 36:36.528
When an uneducated orphan kills someone…

36:38.279 --> 36:40.323
this is what she gets.

36:41.574 --> 36:42.992
That's just how it is.

36:44.327 --> 36:45.745
Why should it be like that?

36:45.829 --> 36:48.540
Who are they to punish you?

36:51.042 --> 36:53.378
I've lied my whole life.

36:54.421 --> 36:56.881
Then you should be punished for just that.

36:57.549 --> 37:00.218
People shouldn't disrespect others
like that.

37:02.679 --> 37:05.640
You can come clean about the lies.

37:06.141 --> 37:08.143
It sucks, but you can set things right.

37:08.226 --> 37:09.602
I'll help you.

37:17.819 --> 37:20.947
No one helps others for no reason.

37:22.282 --> 37:24.826
That's the one thing I've learned in life.

37:26.703 --> 37:28.747
Maybe you still have more to learn.

37:29.330 --> 37:31.082
You only just met me.

37:36.463 --> 37:37.589
Ms. Ro-sa.

37:38.423 --> 37:39.758
Don't give up.

37:40.383 --> 37:42.135
You never know what might happen.

37:42.719 --> 37:43.720
Okay?

38:11.664 --> 38:12.707
Wow.

38:13.625 --> 38:15.960
I've never been to an observatory before.

38:17.629 --> 38:19.047
Me neither.

38:21.716 --> 38:24.844
I thought we should wrap up the day
by looking at the stars.

38:26.554 --> 38:30.183
I feel like we've been doing a lot
of stargazing ever since we first met.

38:32.727 --> 38:34.771
What was it you wanted to talk about?

38:34.854 --> 38:36.606
Something about "that option."

38:40.735 --> 38:45.240
It doesn't matter anymore.
I heard you're going to the States.

38:46.658 --> 38:48.701
I haven't decided yet.

38:49.410 --> 38:52.831
How could you just disappear like that
without even hearing me out?

38:54.707 --> 38:56.501
Why are you undecided?

38:56.584 --> 38:59.754
I haven't heard the details,
but it seems like a good opportunity.

39:02.006 --> 39:04.968
Because I haven't discussed it
with my business partner yet.

39:05.677 --> 39:08.680
I'm not the type to juggle
two different things at once.

39:09.472 --> 39:11.641
I wanted to look you in the eye,

39:11.724 --> 39:13.142
talk things through,

39:14.269 --> 39:16.646
and then decide.

39:22.110 --> 39:23.111
So…

39:25.071 --> 39:26.990
have you made up your mind?

39:34.998 --> 39:37.000
I didn't realize it until you asked…

39:39.586 --> 39:41.087
but I guess I want to go.

39:47.093 --> 39:48.636
You've made the right call.

39:50.096 --> 39:52.473
Duson-ri isn't big enough
for someone like you.

39:52.557 --> 39:54.767
You should go back to where you belong.

39:58.646 --> 39:59.898
What about you?

40:00.607 --> 40:02.692
You haven't said what you're going to do.

40:03.735 --> 40:08.448
I'll finish what I need to do on my end
and then think about it.

40:09.991 --> 40:12.660
I can't juggle two things at once either.

40:17.624 --> 40:19.375
When you're done…

40:20.668 --> 40:22.629
do you want to keep working with me?

40:24.547 --> 40:26.591
But you're going to the States.

40:28.843 --> 40:30.970
Yes. In the States.

40:43.900 --> 40:46.444
…and even the restaurant
she ran to make a living.

40:47.070 --> 40:51.324
The fake Kim Ro-sa took
everything the real one left behind.

40:52.200 --> 40:53.242
Ma'am.

40:54.118 --> 40:58.206
I need you to tell me
which parts of the story are true

40:59.082 --> 41:00.500
and which aren't.

41:03.419 --> 41:06.047
It's not like they made it all up.

41:07.048 --> 41:11.219
Even in a single case,
there can be multiple perspectives.

41:11.302 --> 41:13.721
But your side of the story
matters the most to me.

41:14.681 --> 41:16.724
So feel free to talk.

41:19.352 --> 41:20.478
Gosh.

41:27.235 --> 41:29.904
I don't even know where to begin…

41:32.115 --> 41:34.575
I've never told anyone before.

41:37.203 --> 41:38.538
And to you…

41:40.331 --> 41:42.333
it might sound bizarre.

41:43.793 --> 41:46.504
We're not here to judge your life.

41:46.587 --> 41:48.047
We're here to help.

41:48.589 --> 41:52.218
But to do that, as your lawyer,
I need to know the whole story.

41:57.849 --> 41:58.975
Ma'am.

41:59.517 --> 42:00.601
It's okay.

42:01.853 --> 42:03.146
Take your time.

42:10.611 --> 42:12.447
My real name…

42:13.573 --> 42:15.199
is Hyeon Sang-wol.

42:18.953 --> 42:21.748
Ro-sa and I were very different.

42:22.290 --> 42:25.960
Ro-sa was the neighborhood genius,

42:27.211 --> 42:29.047
whereas I couldn't read…

42:29.922 --> 42:31.883
even after finishing elementary school.

42:35.011 --> 42:37.388
I'd learned the alphabet,

42:39.098 --> 42:41.392
but for some reason,
I just couldn't do it.

42:42.435 --> 42:44.687
So I only worked jobs
where I didn't have to read.

42:44.771 --> 42:46.773
It was written right there
on the envelope.

42:46.856 --> 42:48.733
How could you not know
there was money inside?

42:48.816 --> 42:51.360
- I faced unfair situations…
- The foreman said…

42:51.444 --> 42:55.114
- …but I did my best to hide it.
- …you were the last one at the office!

42:55.198 --> 42:56.741
Where did you hide the money?

42:56.824 --> 42:59.077
People forgave a thief…

42:59.160 --> 43:01.412
- Forget it.
- …but not being able to read…

43:01.496 --> 43:03.039
You put the money back.

43:03.122 --> 43:06.667
- …made you less than human.
- If you can't, call the police right now!

43:06.751 --> 43:08.586
What do you think you're doing?

43:08.669 --> 43:10.129
Who are you?

43:10.213 --> 43:13.091
Sang-wol, get up.

43:13.716 --> 43:16.177
- Only Ro-sa knew everything…
- Are you okay?

43:16.260 --> 43:18.137
I'm sorry I came too late.

43:18.221 --> 43:19.931
…and never let go of my hand.

43:21.349 --> 43:22.600
Sorry.

43:22.683 --> 43:24.602
The autumn leaves
Have had their moment

43:24.685 --> 43:26.813
- And now, everywhere I walk
- Okay, smile.

43:26.896 --> 43:27.814
The ground is soft

43:27.897 --> 43:30.608
- One, two. That's lovely.
- With freshly fallen leaves

43:30.691 --> 43:32.276
"Plum Blossoms in Winter."

43:32.902 --> 43:35.238
- I'm only renting this house
- The book she read…

43:35.321 --> 43:36.322
The yard is filled with

43:36.405 --> 43:38.908
- Six or seven kinds of trees
- The first poem she wrote…

43:38.991 --> 43:40.201
Persimmon, jujube

43:40.284 --> 43:43.538
- Cherry, and grape for fruit
- Even the meaning of my name…

43:43.621 --> 43:45.957
- And lilac, rose
- Ro-sa read them all to me.

43:46.040 --> 43:48.334
- And wisteria for flowers
- Next person!

43:48.960 --> 43:51.254
Smile. One, two…

43:52.839 --> 43:54.048
One more!

43:55.258 --> 43:57.135
Are you two sisters or friends?

43:58.636 --> 44:00.012
We're twins!

44:00.096 --> 44:01.722
No wonder you look alike.

44:03.057 --> 44:04.475
All right, then.

44:04.559 --> 44:07.311
- Isn't this fun?
- One, two…

44:13.818 --> 44:15.194
APRIL 12, 1974
RO-SA AND SANG-WOL

44:21.701 --> 44:22.869
Hey!

44:23.578 --> 44:25.746
- What?
- You should've called me.

44:25.830 --> 44:26.873
- Goodness.
- My gosh.

44:28.166 --> 44:29.667
Let's have some steamed buns.

44:29.750 --> 44:32.795
We lived together
after we left the orphanage.

44:33.921 --> 44:34.881
It's so good.

44:34.964 --> 44:36.883
Those were good times.

44:38.801 --> 44:40.845
When it was just the two of us,

44:40.928 --> 44:43.055
- nothing felt wrong.
- Eat some more.

44:45.266 --> 44:46.309
KIM RO-SA

44:56.736 --> 44:58.696
Are you insane? Why are you burning this?

44:59.947 --> 45:01.199
What's wrong?

45:01.282 --> 45:03.576
She's burning the poem you wrote, Ro-sa.

45:05.036 --> 45:07.079
I told her she could.
I already memorized it.

45:08.456 --> 45:09.582
Let's go.

45:09.665 --> 45:10.750
I'm sorry.

45:14.921 --> 45:16.631
I only realized that…

45:17.590 --> 45:19.508
once others started moving in with us.

45:20.509 --> 45:22.929
- Cheers!
- Cheers.

45:23.012 --> 45:25.139
- Cheers!
- We have so much to eat.

45:28.559 --> 45:31.020
Ro-sa, your poetry…

45:31.896 --> 45:33.731
lacks the current zeitgeist.

45:34.273 --> 45:36.192
If you just want to write pretty lines,

45:36.275 --> 45:38.486
- then write children's poems.
- I agree.

45:40.446 --> 45:42.573
What felt natural to us…

45:42.657 --> 45:43.991
I guess so.

45:44.075 --> 45:47.745
…seemed flawed to the rest of the world.

45:47.828 --> 45:49.163
That's why…

45:51.582 --> 45:53.042
I like Ro-sa's poems.

45:54.835 --> 45:57.296
Wait. What's going on here?

45:57.380 --> 45:59.715
- What do you think?
- What's between you two?

45:59.799 --> 46:00.800
- Nothing's going on.
- Hey…

46:00.883 --> 46:02.969
- It's not nothing. Have a drink.
- No.

46:03.594 --> 46:05.638
I'm not letting it go
until you tell us!

46:05.721 --> 46:08.015
I was the one who was flawed.

46:10.142 --> 46:11.894
To me, Ro-sa was…

46:38.337 --> 46:41.090
That night, I left the house.

46:41.757 --> 46:44.802
Nothing would be flawed
once I was out of the picture.

46:44.885 --> 46:47.805
Ro-sa begged me not to go,

46:47.888 --> 46:51.517
but I couldn't even tell her why.
I just ran away.

46:51.600 --> 46:54.395
- Thank you. Goodbye.
- Sang-wol! Take this to the table!

46:54.478 --> 46:56.939
Just a moment!
Next customer, please come in.

46:57.023 --> 46:58.607
Ice pops!

46:59.567 --> 47:02.236
I wandered wherever my feet took me

47:03.070 --> 47:04.947
and ended up working at a restaurant.

47:06.449 --> 47:07.783
- Sang-wol.
- Yes?

47:07.867 --> 47:09.910
- I learned the recipe back then.
- Come here.

47:09.994 --> 47:11.037
Two spoons.

47:11.120 --> 47:14.582
- No one wanted chicken giblets.
- One spoon of soy sauce,

47:14.665 --> 47:16.292
half a spoon of doenjang and gochujang.

47:16.375 --> 47:18.336
- So I could always get my share.
- Good.

47:21.172 --> 47:23.549
I couldn't help myself…

47:24.884 --> 47:27.094
so I called Ro-sa just once.

47:27.678 --> 47:28.804
Ro-sa?

47:29.305 --> 47:31.891
She moved after getting married.
Haven't you heard?

47:39.398 --> 47:40.900
I figured as much.

47:42.276 --> 47:43.944
Ro-sa always…

47:45.446 --> 47:47.865
wanted a family.

48:05.549 --> 48:07.385
Years passed.

48:07.927 --> 48:09.512
I went to Seoul on an errand…

48:09.595 --> 48:11.680
- It's good, right?
- So good.

48:11.764 --> 48:13.974
…and ran into her by chance.

48:16.394 --> 48:17.812
- Thanks. Come again.
- Thank you.

48:17.895 --> 48:19.772
- I should take a look at this.
- Go ahead.

48:19.855 --> 48:21.649
Can I get two steamed buns?

48:21.732 --> 48:23.067
- Two?
- Yes.

48:23.734 --> 48:26.028
Let me get you the warmest ones.

48:34.203 --> 48:35.204
Ro-sa?

48:37.206 --> 48:38.624
Are you Ro-sa?

48:43.129 --> 48:44.130
Sang-wol.

48:46.382 --> 48:47.883
How long has it been?

48:48.426 --> 48:51.554
I heard you married Jong-su!
Now you have a child?

48:52.054 --> 48:54.640
Let's go somewhere warm and catch up…

49:07.862 --> 49:10.364
Ro-sa was being abused.

49:13.617 --> 49:15.578
Even when she was pregnant.

49:18.289 --> 49:21.792
She blamed herself
until the day she died,

49:21.876 --> 49:23.836
thinking her child's condition
was her fault.

49:24.879 --> 49:26.088
Did you report it?

49:26.630 --> 49:28.215
Did you not go to the police?

49:30.092 --> 49:31.719
Back then,

49:31.802 --> 49:34.805
if you ran to a station begging for help,

49:34.889 --> 49:38.642
they'd tell you to listen to your husband
and send you home.

49:40.311 --> 49:42.897
All of their friends took his side.

49:44.440 --> 49:46.609
With no family to turn to,

49:46.692 --> 49:49.570
Ro-sa endured it all alone
with no support.

49:52.281 --> 49:54.909
I took her and the child and ran away.

49:56.535 --> 49:58.245
Things were good for a while.

49:59.371 --> 50:01.665
I'd come back from work,

50:02.333 --> 50:04.502
and Ro-sa would be waiting with the baby.

50:09.089 --> 50:10.716
But misery…

50:14.261 --> 50:18.307
isn't something you can
cut off that easily.

50:29.818 --> 50:31.153
Damn you.

50:31.737 --> 50:33.948
- Shit.
- What are you doing?

50:37.409 --> 50:39.578
Damn it!

50:44.166 --> 50:46.544
I never liked you from the start.

50:57.137 --> 50:58.305
Mommy!

51:25.916 --> 51:27.334
Take Yeong-ho and leave.

51:28.502 --> 51:29.545
What?

51:30.421 --> 51:32.506
I killed Cha Jong-su.

51:34.008 --> 51:35.634
What are you saying?

51:36.260 --> 51:37.469
Sang-wol.

51:40.681 --> 51:42.141
Get a grip, Ro-sa.

51:43.726 --> 51:45.811
You have to raise Yeong-ho.

52:04.663 --> 52:08.500
While I was in prison,
Ro-sa suffered even more.

52:10.169 --> 52:13.881
People judged her for siding
with a woman who killed her husband.

52:14.590 --> 52:16.508
Her in-laws cut ties with her.

52:18.052 --> 52:20.763
She raised a child
with special needs on her own.

52:22.097 --> 52:26.602
She even sold her poems
for next to nothing just to get by.

52:28.145 --> 52:31.065
The real problem started
after I was released.

52:32.608 --> 52:37.321
Ro-sa's occasional publishing work
didn't bring in enough to support us.

52:38.364 --> 52:40.115
I had to work,

52:41.283 --> 52:43.452
but word got out that I was a murderer.

52:44.119 --> 52:46.121
No one would hire me.

52:46.205 --> 52:47.373
Ro-sa.

52:55.005 --> 52:57.716
That's when Ro-sa suggested it.

52:58.550 --> 53:00.010
Sang-wol,

53:00.094 --> 53:01.595
let's go to Seoul.

53:02.680 --> 53:05.015
Somewhere no one knows us,

53:05.724 --> 53:07.101
where we can start over.

53:08.686 --> 53:12.064
So, that was when you started
using her name?

53:14.983 --> 53:17.152
Whenever I needed a name for anything,

53:17.861 --> 53:21.323
I used Ro-sa's.

53:22.825 --> 53:26.328
Because I had a criminal record.

53:26.954 --> 53:29.957
Getting a family register,
or opening a bank account…

53:30.040 --> 53:33.627
For anything that needed a name,
we used hers.

53:37.214 --> 53:40.050
After a few years of scraping by,

53:40.884 --> 53:43.053
we finally managed to save enough

53:43.137 --> 53:46.932
to buy a two-story house
that that was listed at a low price.

53:47.015 --> 53:49.727
TITLE DEED
GRANTEE: KIM RO-SA

53:49.810 --> 53:51.770
We'll run a restaurant on the first floor

53:52.396 --> 53:54.189
and live on the second.

53:54.857 --> 53:57.067
It's just down the stairs,

53:57.151 --> 53:59.403
so we can take Yeong-ho
back and forth easily.

54:01.113 --> 54:02.698
What will you name the restaurant?

54:04.199 --> 54:05.743
Kim Ro-sa.

54:06.535 --> 54:08.370
Come on.

54:08.912 --> 54:10.706
It should sound like a real restaurant.

54:10.789 --> 54:13.208
Then Rosa Restaurant?

54:15.210 --> 54:16.295
Rosa Restaurant?

54:16.378 --> 54:19.715
Why does life
always take something away…

54:19.798 --> 54:22.050
- Do you like it?
- …whenever it gives you something?

54:22.134 --> 54:23.051
Look at this.

54:24.386 --> 54:26.722
Ro-sa, are you okay?

54:26.805 --> 54:29.725
- She had cancer.
- Why is no one coming here to help her?

54:30.726 --> 54:33.604
- By the time she saw a doctor…
- Hang in there.

54:33.687 --> 54:36.273
…it was already too late to do anything.

54:39.568 --> 54:41.737
You're not well.
Where did you go all alone?

54:44.281 --> 54:45.657
I admitted Yeong-ho.

54:46.867 --> 54:50.037
What? Did you really leave him
at that place?

54:54.291 --> 54:56.710
You can't run the restaurant
and look after him by yourself.

54:56.794 --> 54:58.420
Why would I be by myself?

54:59.046 --> 55:01.632
Stop talking about dying
and get treatment.

55:06.261 --> 55:08.013
This is a death report form.

55:08.889 --> 55:11.433
- Ro-sa.
- Listen to me.

55:13.227 --> 55:14.561
When I die…

55:15.687 --> 55:17.648
report my death as Hyeon Sang-wol's,

55:18.649 --> 55:20.359
and you live as Kim Ro-sa.

55:20.984 --> 55:22.110
Are you crazy?

55:22.861 --> 55:24.530
How could I live under your name?

55:26.156 --> 55:28.200
How could I live as you?

55:28.283 --> 55:29.701
Then what about Yeong-ho?

55:31.411 --> 55:33.747
Besides me, the only family he has
is Cha Jong-su's family.

55:33.831 --> 55:38.001
And you know they don't care about
what happens to him.

55:39.920 --> 55:41.630
When I die,

55:41.713 --> 55:45.300
they'll take him for the money
and abandon him without a second thought.

55:47.386 --> 55:48.512
So please…

55:50.430 --> 55:51.974
live as me.

55:54.852 --> 55:56.311
I'm begging you.

56:51.867 --> 56:53.869
TITLE DEED
GRANTEE: KIM RO-SA

56:56.496 --> 56:58.624
These are the things Ro-sa left behind.

56:59.207 --> 57:03.128
I don't know what's written on them,
but I thought they might help.

57:06.882 --> 57:09.593
PROOF OF ADMISSION: CHA YEONG-HO
SEVERE INTELLECTUAL DISABILITY

57:09.676 --> 57:11.595
PUBLISHING RIGHTS AGREEMENTS

57:11.678 --> 57:13.263
GIFT DEED

57:24.608 --> 57:27.152
If you're reading this letter,

57:27.903 --> 57:30.781
it means Sang-wol has finally
found someone to confide in,

57:31.448 --> 57:35.619
or she's desperate enough
to hand this over.

57:37.162 --> 57:42.292
I sincerely hope
that you're someone with a kind heart.

57:43.710 --> 57:45.837
Life is like poetry.

57:45.921 --> 57:48.966
From a distance,
it looks like an indecipherable code,

57:49.675 --> 57:52.427
but if you look closely
with a heart willing to understand,

57:52.511 --> 57:56.390
only then will you see the meaning within.

57:57.516 --> 58:01.645
I spent my whole life trying to define
Sang-wol and me with a single word.

58:02.479 --> 58:04.773
But each word felt
either too grand or too small.

58:05.482 --> 58:07.275
I never found the right one.

58:08.485 --> 58:11.363
Still, you can define
who Hyeon Sang-wol is

58:12.114 --> 58:13.824
in just three syllables.

58:14.992 --> 58:16.994
What will you name the restaurant?

58:17.786 --> 58:18.829
Kim Ro-sa.

58:19.413 --> 58:20.455
Kim Ro-sa.

58:21.832 --> 58:24.001
With that foolishly kind heart of hers,

58:24.835 --> 58:28.463
she took all the bad
so I could have only the good.

58:29.548 --> 58:32.592
All her kindness is held
within the three syllables of my name.

58:34.845 --> 58:38.598
I held onto everything for a while
because the world is harsh and cold.

58:39.433 --> 58:43.437
But everything in my name
truly belongs to Sang-wol.

58:47.107 --> 58:50.277
Now I hope
that she can finally let go of the lies

58:50.360 --> 58:54.031
and reclaim what's hers.

58:56.366 --> 58:59.870
NOTARIZED WILL
TESTATOR: KIM RO-SA

58:59.995 --> 59:02.956
TESTATOR: KIM RO-SA
NOTARY: ATTORNEY AN HYEON-MIN

59:04.374 --> 59:05.542
Please,

59:06.585 --> 59:08.628
look upon this lonely yet kind soul

59:09.671 --> 59:12.132
as you would read a poem.

59:16.344 --> 59:17.429
Ms. Sang-wol!

59:18.889 --> 59:19.931
It's me, Ho-su!

59:20.682 --> 59:22.934
Please open the door just for a second.

59:23.018 --> 59:24.352
Okay.

59:27.397 --> 59:28.815
I came to read it for you.

59:28.899 --> 59:30.650
- What?
- I'll read it for you.

59:31.651 --> 59:33.195
This will fix everything.

59:33.278 --> 59:34.529
What?

59:36.323 --> 59:37.491
We have one strategy.

59:37.574 --> 59:39.785
We'll admit to the identity theft charges.

59:39.868 --> 59:42.204
Right away? We're not fighting it?

59:42.287 --> 59:45.123
There's no need. We have this.

59:45.832 --> 59:47.959
This is the will Kim Ro-sa wrote
before she died.

59:48.043 --> 59:50.837
It's notarized and legally binding.

59:50.921 --> 59:53.590
We admit that she's been living
under Ms. Kim Ro-sa's name,

59:53.673 --> 59:55.967
but since all the assets
were already gifted to her,

59:56.051 --> 59:58.678
it's hard to say she profited
from the identity theft.

01:00:00.263 --> 01:00:02.265
According to the publisher,

01:00:02.349 --> 01:00:04.476
she pretended to be the poet
until recently.

01:00:04.559 --> 01:00:08.105
Wasn't that to take advantage
of royalties and other earnings?

01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:11.149
All income earned as a poet

01:00:11.817 --> 01:00:14.444
was donated in full
to the deceased's alma mater, HNU,

01:00:14.528 --> 01:00:16.988
with Ms. Hyeon contributing
her own funds as well.

01:00:17.072 --> 01:00:19.366
Those are also included in the gift deed.

01:00:21.034 --> 01:00:22.577
CERTIFICATE OF DONATION
KIM RO-SA

01:00:22.661 --> 01:00:25.038
DONATION RECEIPT - DONOR: KIM RO-SA
RECIPIENT: HANKUK NATIONAL UNIVERSITY

01:00:33.130 --> 01:00:35.841
We just met your friend
and admitted to the charges.

01:00:37.425 --> 01:00:40.554
I was wondering how that would go.
Thanks for calling.

01:00:40.637 --> 01:00:42.722
Things won't go as you want them to.

01:00:43.515 --> 01:00:45.183
I called to tell you that.

01:00:57.654 --> 01:00:59.197
Hi, please have one.

01:00:59.281 --> 01:01:00.198
Hello.

01:01:00.282 --> 01:01:02.117
Hi, thank you for your hard work.

01:01:02.200 --> 01:01:03.493
Hello. Thanks for everything.

01:01:03.577 --> 01:01:05.453
- What brings you here?
- Hi, please have one.

01:01:05.537 --> 01:01:07.998
You know the Kim Ro-sa Scholarship
here at HNU

01:01:08.081 --> 01:01:09.749
that's been around for 20 years?

01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:11.168
Hello.

01:01:11.251 --> 01:01:14.921
You received the Kim Ro-sa Scholarship
in college, right?

01:01:17.841 --> 01:01:19.384
That would be great. Thank you.

01:01:19.467 --> 01:01:20.635
DONATION STATEMENT

01:01:20.719 --> 01:01:24.514
The claim that they were a happy family
comes only from the brother-in-law.

01:01:24.598 --> 01:01:26.725
The poet was a victim
of serious domestic violence,

01:01:26.808 --> 01:01:28.476
even while she was pregnant.

01:01:29.144 --> 01:01:31.313
Those people refused
to look after her son,

01:01:31.396 --> 01:01:33.106
using his disability as an excuse.

01:01:33.190 --> 01:01:37.194
I don't understand why
they've waited until now to step up.

01:01:37.277 --> 01:01:40.906
It seems like they're after the deceased's
inheritance and other benefits.

01:01:40.989 --> 01:01:42.991
IF YOU BADMOUTHED HYEON SANG-WOL,
REFLECT ON YOURSELF

01:01:46.578 --> 01:01:49.497
- Hello. Here it is.
- Thank you.

01:01:49.581 --> 01:01:50.582
Good luck!

01:02:04.304 --> 01:02:05.555
Are you okay?

01:02:05.639 --> 01:02:07.682
Should we go in a little later?

01:02:07.766 --> 01:02:09.142
No.

01:02:09.226 --> 01:02:10.685
We can't be late.

01:02:11.436 --> 01:02:14.272
Today will probably be
the last day of questioning.

01:02:14.356 --> 01:02:18.026
No matter how things turn out,
we'll handle it together, just like now.

01:02:18.109 --> 01:02:19.611
Don't worry too much.

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:21.738
Hey, Ho-su!

01:02:21.821 --> 01:02:22.697
PROSECUTION SERVICE

01:02:22.781 --> 01:02:24.366
Wait, take this!

01:02:24.991 --> 01:02:26.117
Here.

01:02:26.201 --> 01:02:29.037
I told you that you didn't have to come.

01:02:30.830 --> 01:02:32.415
What are these?

01:02:33.500 --> 01:02:35.085
They're petitions.

01:02:36.962 --> 01:02:41.007
It's from students who received
the Kim Ro-sa Scholarship.

01:02:41.800 --> 01:02:43.969
They wrote them after hearing about you.

01:02:45.595 --> 01:02:48.515
I'll read them all to you later.

01:02:49.015 --> 01:02:51.309
So good luck, and do your best in there.

01:02:58.400 --> 01:02:59.943
So that's how it went.

01:03:00.443 --> 01:03:02.320
All right. I'll tell her.

01:03:04.197 --> 01:03:06.199
What did they say?

01:03:06.700 --> 01:03:08.159
Suspended indictment.

01:03:09.953 --> 01:03:13.540
- It's a good thing.
- Ms. Sang-wol!

01:03:14.124 --> 01:03:15.417
You've made it through.

01:03:16.376 --> 01:03:19.129
I had a good feeling about today.
I had this dream last night,

01:03:19.212 --> 01:03:21.589
and as soon as I woke up,
I looked up the interpretation.

01:03:21.673 --> 01:03:23.300
It said it was a lucky dream!

01:03:23.383 --> 01:03:24.676
But I didn't want to jinx it,

01:03:24.759 --> 01:03:27.012
so I couldn't even tell you,
and I kept it…

01:03:27.095 --> 01:03:29.264
All right. Calm down.
I'll get you some water.

01:03:29.347 --> 01:03:30.598
- No, I…
- Let me.

01:03:30.682 --> 01:03:32.434
- I'll get it.
- I…

01:03:33.727 --> 01:03:35.312
This is amazing.

01:03:35.812 --> 01:03:37.814
Listen. Here's what I dreamed last night.

01:03:37.897 --> 01:03:40.108
I was fighting a tiger.

01:03:40.191 --> 01:03:41.776
Bare hands. No weapons.

01:03:41.860 --> 01:03:45.071
But the tiger didn't use its teeth either,
and stood up out of the blue,

01:03:45.155 --> 01:03:48.283
took a boxing stance,
and threw the first punch at me.

01:03:48.366 --> 01:03:49.743
I took the punch. And guess what?

01:03:49.826 --> 01:03:52.787
On the day you closed my book and left,

01:03:52.871 --> 01:03:55.582
Ro-sa, you said to me…

01:03:57.208 --> 01:03:59.002
Don't leave me behind.

01:04:01.629 --> 01:04:03.923
How can I live without you?

01:04:05.175 --> 01:04:06.968
You'll meet…

01:04:09.387 --> 01:04:11.181
…good people.

01:04:12.474 --> 01:04:14.184
There's no one else.

01:04:16.686 --> 01:04:19.564
You're all I have.

01:04:26.988 --> 01:04:29.032
You'll meet them.

01:04:29.657 --> 01:04:32.535
It might take a while, but one day,

01:04:34.329 --> 01:04:37.248
you'll meet people who will read you…

01:04:39.250 --> 01:04:40.710
for who you are.

01:04:56.351 --> 01:04:58.144
It specifically said I'd win a lawsuit.

01:04:58.228 --> 01:05:00.980
It's a suspended indictment, not a win.

01:05:01.815 --> 01:05:06.069
Whatever. You should go and buy a cake.
Let's have a party.

01:05:06.152 --> 01:05:07.779
It might take a while…

01:05:07.862 --> 01:05:09.155
Sweet potato cake, maybe?

01:05:09.239 --> 01:05:11.032
- …but one day…
- Let's ask her.

01:05:11.116 --> 01:05:14.994
…you'll meet people
who will read you for who you are.

01:05:21.209 --> 01:05:23.795
Everyone loves
sweet potato cake in Duson-ri.

01:05:23.878 --> 01:05:26.464
- Let's see who wins.
- Fine.

01:05:27.048 --> 01:05:29.467
- Ms. Sang-wol.
- Ms. Sang-wol.

01:05:30.009 --> 01:05:32.178
Do you prefer sweet potato
or strawberry?

01:05:33.304 --> 01:05:34.389
For cake.

01:05:34.472 --> 01:05:36.224
- Strawberry.
- I told you!

01:05:47.277 --> 01:05:49.070
RING

01:05:50.113 --> 01:05:51.239
Hello.

01:05:56.995 --> 01:05:58.163
Hello?

01:05:59.664 --> 01:06:01.833
Hello? Hello?

01:06:18.892 --> 01:06:20.268
Why aren't you coming in?

01:06:29.319 --> 01:06:31.654
Is something wrong?

01:06:40.830 --> 01:06:42.999
I need to take this call real quick.

01:07:32.590 --> 01:07:33.758
YU MI-RAE - YU MI-JI

01:07:33.841 --> 01:07:35.677
I'm calling from the hospital.

01:07:35.760 --> 01:07:37.303
Are you Ms. Kang Wol-sun's daughter?

01:07:37.387 --> 01:07:38.846
We're from the Fair Trade Commission.

01:07:38.930 --> 01:07:41.724
We're investigating the Sihan Construction
case, so please cooperate.

01:07:41.808 --> 01:07:44.561
More importantly,
you're here now.

01:07:44.644 --> 01:07:47.647
That must mean you're ready
to respond to my offer.

01:07:47.730 --> 01:07:50.400
I want to see things through
to the very end here.

01:07:50.942 --> 01:07:52.443
You're sick again, aren't you?

01:07:52.527 --> 01:07:54.028
Let me see if you have a fever.

01:07:54.112 --> 01:07:55.697
I'm just a bit tired.

01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:56.698
Let's meet up tomorrow.

01:07:57.699 --> 01:07:59.659
What should I do now?

01:07:59.742 --> 01:08:02.579
You mean there's nothing I can do
until things get worse?

01:08:03.580 --> 01:08:05.123
Here's what I dreamed last night.

01:08:05.206 --> 01:08:07.041
I was fighting a tiger.

01:08:07.125 --> 01:08:08.835
Bare hands. No weapons.

01:08:08.918 --> 01:08:12.130
But the tiger didn't use its teeth either,
and stood up out of the blue,

01:08:12.213 --> 01:08:15.383
took a boxing stance,
and threw the first punch at me.

01:08:15.466 --> 01:08:18.052
I took the punch.
And guess what? It was soft.

01:08:18.136 --> 01:08:20.972
And it didn't hurt. Total kitty punch.

01:08:21.055 --> 01:08:23.266
So I grabbed it by the scruff,

01:08:23.349 --> 01:08:25.435
slammed it down, and beat it up.

01:08:25.518 --> 01:08:26.978
So you hit an animal?

01:08:27.061 --> 01:08:28.313
Yes.

01:08:29.230 --> 01:08:32.025
But it was a really mean tiger.

01:08:32.108 --> 01:08:34.068
Like the uncle from The Lion King.

01:08:34.152 --> 01:08:37.238
Right. The lion, I mean, tiger.

01:08:37.322 --> 01:08:38.740
So it was a lucky dream?

01:08:38.823 --> 01:08:40.116
That's the thing.

01:08:40.199 --> 01:08:42.327
I looked it up,
and it's not just any lucky dream.

01:08:42.410 --> 01:08:44.787
It specifically said I'd win a lawsuit.

01:08:44.871 --> 01:08:46.623
You shouldn't get ahead of yourself.

01:08:46.706 --> 01:08:48.916
It's a suspended indictment, not a win.

01:08:49.709 --> 01:08:54.130
Whatever. You should go and buy a cake.
Let's have a party.

01:08:58.051 --> 01:09:00.053
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
